WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Good morning John! It's my last Pizzamas
video. I can't beli...it went by so fast.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.320
Though it was a very long couple of weeks.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.400
It had happy times and sad times and reunion videos

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.790
and charity galas and now I'm in New
Hampshire visiting family and I want to

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.510
be clear that this is an unusual level
of weird. However, I would be lying if I

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.810
said that my life hasn't gotten really
weird and really cool and really

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:25.380
wonderful and really complicated over
the last eight or nine years of us

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.750
making VlogBrothers videos. My life is
not normal. I don't think any lives are

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.160
normal, but my life is clearly not normal
and I am a number of things that I was

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.719
not in 2006. I and professionally
respected, fairly well known, and

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:41.039
thus one might say that I am a success.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.820
Ever since people have started to say this to me
that like "what's it like to be

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.300
successful ? " or "Congratulations on your
success". I have felt really weird about it.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.340
Troubled by it and I was having a hard
time figuring out exactly why I was

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:56.590
feeling this way. Is it modesty? Is
it false modesty? Maybe a bit of both of those.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.800
But after thinking about this for a while.
Here's what it actually is. I feel like

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.809
when someone says "congratulations on
your success" they're putting you into a

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:08.529
category of people that...that is
extremely difficult to achieve.

00:01:08.529 --> 00:01:12.029
That only a very small percentage of humans on the
planet could ever achieve

00:01:12.029 --> 00:01:15.429
and then saying that that is a thing that all
people should strive for.

00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:18.840
Despite the fact that the only way that something
like this can happen to you is if

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:23.580
happened to stumble across a great big
pile of steaming luck and then fall into

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.470
it and get stuck all over your body and it's like... I can't get this luck off of me!

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:32.670
There isn't enough space in human brains
for everyone to be known by a large

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:36.030
number of people. And that's what fame is. Weirdly, it's just the ability to have

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:41.120
your face recognized by a larger than
average number of people....Yeah.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.200
Look, I'm very happy. I'm a happy person. But I was happy before I was "successful".

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:49.320
I was happy in 2006. I had great
friends in great family and I was

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.140
working on interesting projects and I
had learned a lot of things and I was

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.000
excited to learn more and I don't think
that most people would even argue that

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.800
success is a necessary part of happiness. But I think we do conflate those two things.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:03.640
And whenever I am told that I'm successful. I worry
about what that word means to the person

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.119
saying it and what it means to society. Does it mean achieving the things

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:10.379
you want to achieve? Which is the good
definition.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.040
I want to do things and then I did do

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:16.910
those things and thus I am a success. I
have succeeded. Or is it achieving

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:21.640
something that most people implicitly
cannot achieve. It is impossible for most

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.760
people to have because it's based on the
scarcity of resources. It's based on the

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.140
fact that not everyone can be famous.
It's based on the fact that not everyone

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.020
can be in the top twenty percent of
income.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.720
Is being successful being richer or more powerful or more well known

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.820
than most people? That kind of societally recognized

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.740
implicit success is something
that I think we all crave and it is

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.960
something that I have to some extent... but
I don't think it's something that I need

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.750
to feel valued and valuable and it's not
something that I... it's definitely not

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:54.260
something I need to feel happy. I think that it
is very societally important that we

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.900
figure out ways to value ourselves and
value each other that don't have

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.200
anything to do with scarcity. You know
the scarcity of money,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.660
the scarcity of of fame, the scarcity of power even.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.480
I would much rather be and much rather associate myself with

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.980
the kind of people who want
to have a positive impact on a small

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:15.590
number of people. Than to collect a great
deal of wealth and power even at the

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.530
expense of other people. So John. As I finish off
my final Pizzamas video of 2015.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:24.060
I don't know what "success" is! I still don't.
I know what "successes" are.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:29.060
Individual things. But the the acquisition of
success and "being a success" I think

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.430
that's kind of a made up thing. But I am very
grateful. What I'm grateful for is having

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.230
great friends and great family and a
great community who make me feel valued

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.910
who make me question myself and
question my beliefs and challenge me

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:44.800
to do interesting and difficult things...
and to become a better person.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.300
John, I'll see you on Tuesday... Or No!
Friday I'll see you tomorrow!

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.260
Which means, yes! We only have one day left of Pizzamas.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.840
One day left for to get the shirts and the other products at DFTBA.com

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.480
and thank you to everybody for a really great Pizzamas.

